          "date": "2026-11-13 12:30:18.000000000",
          "tz": 600
        },
        "subject": "DRAFT LU-21180 kunit: add optional kmemleak check to ku",
        "message": "DRAFT LU-21180 kunit: add optional kmemleak check to ku\n\nAdd support to catch memory leaked by a kunit module's test run.\n\n-k requires a kernel with kmemleak enabled; it is off by\ndefault since forcing a scan is slow.\n\nBefore loading a module ku clears kmemleak's list of suspected\nleaks, and after unloading it waits for kmemleak's minimum object\nage (MSECS_MIN_AGE, 5s in mm/kmemleak.c: an object is not reported\nas unreferenced until it has been allocated at least that long)\nbefore triggering a scan and reading the list back, failing the test\nif anything is reported. Scanning right after rmmod without this\ndelay misses this run's leaks (they are too young to be reported)\nand only surfaces them, misattributed, on a later run. This scopes\nthe check to just that module's load/unload instead of whatever\nkmemleak had already logged elsewhere.\n\nThe sleep plus the forced scan add 6+ seconds per module regardless\nof what is loaded, so -k is not meant for routine fast test runs.\n\nAlso fail early with a clear message if ku is not run as root, since\ninsmod/rmmod of the test modules need it anyway, rather than letting\ninsmod fail partway through the run.\n\nExample, a leaked 64-byte allocation from lod_comp_prep_create():\n\n  unreferenced object 0xffff913f809e1680 (size 64):\n    comm \"kunit_try_catch\", pid 3316, jiffies 4295099075 (age 18.455s)\n    hex dump (first 32 bytes):\n      00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................\n      00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................\n    backtrace:\n      [<00000000eae94f93>] kmalloc_trace+0x25/0xa0\n      [<00000000cb6aca88>] lod_comp_prep_create+0x198/0x1980 [lod]\n      [<000000000ebbc798>] 0xffffffffc190b410\n      [<000000001e467737>] 0xffffffffc190b6f7\n      [<000000007b9a4303>] kunit_generic_run_threadfn_adapter+0x13/0x30 [kunit]\n      [<00000000a1a25ad0>] kthread+0xdd/0x100\n      [<00000000e623718c>] ret_from_fork+0x29/0x50\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: AGENT:Claude Sonnet 5.0 [Augment Code]\nChange-Id: I6cade09bd6b26f8b82e072f580d3233ec36cd027\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
